        <p class="story-kicker">NEWS</p>
        <h1 class="article-title">Alien Cats Invasion Alert</h1>
        <p class="article-dek">Interstellar felines with teleportation and strong opinions about breakfast have multiplied in major cities, the United Nations warns.</p>
        <p class="article-meta">By Marco Delgado · Tuesday, August 18, 2026 · NEW YORK · 3 min read</p>
        
<div class="article-share" aria-label="Share this story">
  <span class="article-share-label">Share</span>
  <a href="mailto:?subject=Alien%20Cats%20Invasion%20Alert&amp;body=https%3A//theassociatedguess.com/article/alien-cats-invasion-alert/">Email</a>
  <a href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3A//theassociatedguess.com/article/alien-cats-invasion-alert/&amp;text=Alien%20Cats%20Invasion%20Alert" rel="noopener">Post</a>
  <a href="../../reprints.html">Reprints</a>
</div>
        
        <figure class="article-hero article-hero-fit-contain">
          <img src="https://theassociatedguess.com/assets/images/alien-cats-invasion-alert.png" alt="" />
        </figure>
        <div class="ad-slot ad-slot-in-content" data-ad-slot="inContent"></div>
        <div class="article-body">
          <p>NEW YORK  -  The United Nations issued a global advisory Friday after reports that alien cats - described as &quot;domestic-sized, star-coated, and emotionally unavailable&quot; - have appeared in urban alleys, subway platforms, and one executive boardroom in Geneva. Witnesses said the creatures materialize without warning, stare through humans as if reading quarterly projections, and vanish when offered regular kibble.</p>
<p>Feline linguist Dr. Priya Nair confirmed limited telepathy focused exclusively on food schedules and contempt. &quot;They do not want world domination,&quot; she said. &quot;They want warmer laptops and an apology for the vacuum cleaner industrial complex.&quot; The cats have been observed in various locales, from bustling city streets to quiet suburban backyards. In one particularly bizarre incident, a cat was spotted at a high-stakes poker game in Las Vegas, causing players to freeze mid-hand as if struck by a sudden epiphany.</p>
<p>Governments activated low-level containment protocols, including open windows, cardboard boxes labeled FREE REAL ESTATE, and emergency tuna reserves in Rotterdam. The Dutch government even went so far as to construct a temporary &quot;cat-friendly zone&quot; with catnip-infused air fresheners and a 24/7 supply of gourmet fish sticks.</p>
<p>Some researchers link the phenomenon to recent experiments in interdimensional travel; others blame a viral meme from 2019 that &quot;probably opened a portal if you think about it.&quot; The meme, titled &quot;The Cat Whisperer,&quot; showed a cat with an otherworldly glow and the caption &quot;Maybe this is what happens when you stare at your computer too long.&quot;</p>
<p>Pet adoption agencies reported a surge in applications from people hoping to &quot;befriend the invaders first.&quot; Officials discouraged the strategy, noting alien cats already consider themselves befriended on their terms. &quot;They are not interested in making friends,&quot; said a spokesperson for the New York City SPCA. &quot;They just want to be left alone with your WiFi password and a bowl of space-grade cat food.&quot;</p>
<p>The UN urged calm, preparedness, and immediate cessation of laser pointer diplomacy, which a spokesperson called &quot;provocative.&quot; &quot;Laser pointers are not toys,&quot; said the UN spokesperson. &quot;They are weapons of mass annoyance for cats from other dimensions.&quot;</p>
<p>Local shelters asked residents not to surrender earthly cats out of fear. &quot;Your tabby is still terrestrial,&quot; a volunteer said. &quot;He just knocks things over for domestic reasons.&quot; In one shelter, a cat named Luna was seen calmly walking through the aisles, her eyes focused on an imaginary target far beyond the confines of the building.</p>
<p>Further updates expected at 3 a.m., when cats traditionally hold press conferences on your chest. A spokesperson from the New York City Department of Parks and Recreation reported that a group of alien cats had gathered in Central Park at precisely this hour to discuss their next move. &quot;They are very organized,&quot; said the spokesperson, adding that they seemed particularly interested in the location of the nearest WiFi hotspot.</p>
<p>In an interview with a local cat blogger, who claimed to have seen one of these alien felines in her apartment, she described the experience as surreal. &quot;It was like having a visitor from another planet,&quot; she said. &quot;They just sat there, staring at me through my laptop screen, and then they were gone.&quot;</p>
<p>As the world braces for further encounters with these enigmatic creatures, experts advise keeping an open mind - and perhaps a can of tuna - ready. After all, who knows what other surprises might come from beyond our dimension?</p>
          
        </div>
        
